            },
            "reviewBody": "Exactly what I was looking for",
            "datePublished": "2023-01-17T16:56:08.215Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "InTheKitch"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Super easy. Don't even have to cool it off, just skim the solids off the top and don't pour the white liquid at the bottom. Added the lemon zest too.",
            "datePublished": "2021-06-06T02:09:42.153Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "jackj"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is clarified butter, but there's disagreement as to that is the \"drawn butter\" which should be used with lobster/seafood. Some authors insist that plain melted butter is the \"drawn butter\" to be used.\n\nAlso, it is not the same as Ghee, used in Indian recipes, as one commenter suggested. Ghee is indeed clarified, but for much longer - about :30 - so that the browned solids in the bottom flavor the clarified butter/Ghee, and also that more water evaporates out of it.",
            "datePublished": "2020-12-27T19:07:34.030Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jimmy Vandergriff"
            },
            "reviewBody": "No changes and I will make it again",
            "datePublished": "2019-05-28T23:10:44.663Z"
